wsi/metal, anv: VK_EXT_metal_surface swapchains on IOSurfaces for drivers that do not render through Metal (ANV on macOS over B580.kext)

Upstream's Metal WSI (wsi_common_metal.c) has two image paths: KosmicKrisp, whose VkImages are MTLTextures that get a
CAMetalDrawable bound at acquire and a blit into it, and software drivers, whose CPU image is blitted into a drawable by
a Metal command queue. Neither fits a hardware driver with its own GPU memory: the first needs the driver to be Metal,
the second copies every frame through the CPU.

This adds a third path, chosen when the driver fills wsi_device::iosurface:
- every swapchain image is an IOSurface ('BGRA', sRGB-tagged) and the VkImage is a linear (DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
  explicit row pitch) image in that IOSurface's GPU memory: wsi_memory_allocate_info::iosurface_id asks the driver for
  it. ANV gets it from B580.kext (DRM_B580_SURFACE_VRAM CREATE): the one VRAM backing the window server's Metal plugin
  imports too, so the application renders into the memory the compositor reads; no copy anywhere.
- present is at submission: the present's per-image fence is attached to the IOSurface as its write fence
  (DRM_B580_SURFACE_FENCE_ATTACH, the dma-resv model), the VRAM copy is marked newer than the pages (SURFACE_DIRTY, for
  CPU readers) and the plugin's VRAM tag ("NVMTLVramAt:p0" = the new seed) is bumped, then the IOSurface becomes the
  contents of a sublayer filling the CAMetalLayer (one CATransaction, no animation, flushed). The window server's GPU
  waits for the frame; nobody's CPU does.
- acquire hands back the least recently shown image that no other process uses (IOSurfaceIsInUse: the window server
  dropped it) after its GPU readers finished (DRM_B580_SURFACE_FENCE_WAIT, writer).
- IMMEDIATE shows at present; MAILBOX (new) and FIFO latch at the display's refresh (CVDisplayLink): MAILBOX the newest
  frame whose rendering is done (older finished frames go back to the application at once; MAILBOX swapchains get at
  least 4 images), FIFO the oldest, one per refresh. Present ID / present wait signal when a frame is shown.
- MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=buffer forces the page-copy path; MESA_VK_WSI_FPS_LOG=<file> appends a line every 2 s (presents,
  shown and dropped frames per second, acquire time).
- the refresh latch runs on its own thread, woken by the CVDisplayLink; without one (no active display: the screen
  asleep, a remote session) or when its callbacks stop, it ticks every 1/60 s (2/60 s with a silent link) instead of
  failing the present with VK_ERROR_SURFACE_LOST_KHR.
- when the kernel has no shared VRAM for the IOSurface (debug.b580.surfvram 0, budget spent) the swapchain is made
  again with private images copied into the IOSurfaces' pages by the GPU at present (the common buffer blit, pages
  imported as host memory), still present at submission.
ANV: ANV_USE_WSI_PLATFORM with VK_USE_PLATFORM_METAL_EXT, VK_EXT_metal_surface, the three wsi_device::iosurface hooks
(anv_nvmtl_surface.c) and the iosurface_id import in vkAllocateMemory (uncompressed, not scan-out, never mapped).
Build with -Dplatforms=macos (links QuartzCore, Metal, IOSurface, CoreVideo, CoreGraphics).

